pub fn posterior(prior: f64, sensitivity: f64, false_positive: f64) -> Option<f64> {
    if ![prior, sensitivity, false_positive]
        .iter()
        .all(|&p| p.is_finite() && (0.0..=1.0).contains(&p))
    {
        return None;
    }

    let true_positive = sensitivity * prior;
    let denominator = true_positive + false_positive * (1.0 - prior);
    if denominator == 0.0 {
        return None;
    }

    Some(true_positive / denominator)
}
```

Behavior: non-finite or out-of-range inputs return `None`; a zero denominator (e.g. `sensitivity = 0` and either `prior = 1` or `false_positive = 0`) returns `None`. Public API and existing tests are unchanged.

